        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction showed that quantum information can be protected against noise in principle, a conceptual step essential to scalable quantum computation.",
        "attribution": "These names capture key, distinct contributions to early codes and fault-tolerant quantum computing, though the wider development involved many researchers.",
        "maturity": "The theoretical foundations are durable, and experimental demonstrations have advanced substantially; useful large-scale fault-tolerant machines remain unrealized.",
